{
  "_schema": "`<slug>.<vault|portfolio>` -> array of SPEC ids (R# required-difference rows, or the clause id C130 where no R row exists). Read by ExportDiffHarnessTests (Q433, C5): a v2 export that differs from goldens/v1-export/<key>.md on a key listed here is expected-different; the SAME key with no diff is a matched-bug (fail); a diff on an unlisted key is unexplained (fail). The C130/R51 ids on `.portfolio` keys must equal v1's own frontmatter breaches exactly (testV1PortfolioFrontmatterBreachesAreExactlyTheRegisteredRows).",
  "_notes": {
    "C130": "v1's portfolio frontmatter breaches C130: `title:` is written on every note though C130 allows it only when HE gave one (the corpus rows are unpolished, so it is the row's filename stem), and `url:` / `book:` / `chapter:` / `bookAuthor:` are keys outside the C130 list; pic-at-start (body opens with [[img_001]]) exports with its closing `---` fused onto the first sentence and skriftID/skriftHash lost, on BOTH profiles (found by Q433). No R row exists for these; the clause is the registration.",
    "R51": "`people:` written inline (`people: [[A]], [[B]]`) instead of a block list of plain names; and cap-image-no-words' `![[…]]` embed on the portfolio.",
    "D12": "Export v2 (Q434) writes `created:` (the note's createdAt, local date-time like editedAt) and `duration:` (whole seconds of the recording, empty for a note without one) on every vault export, after `editedAt:` (D12, C56, R38). The portfolio's key list (C130) has neither.",
    "C25": "Export v2 (Q434) writes the C25 ladder's title in `title:`, the same one the file is named by; v1 wrote the row's filename stem (`memo_<UUID>`, `capture_<UUID>`, the bare UUID) for a note without a polished title. One line always (a text capture's derived title kept its line breaks).",
    "R38": "Export v2 (Q434): a `.file` capture's shared document goes with the note, named by the note's stem (Documents/ in the vault, beside the note on the portfolio): a PDF embedded, any other file linked.",
    "R50": "Export v2 (Q434): a tag never carries Obsidian's leading `#` (in YAML a bare `- #studio` is a comment, an empty tag), a vault tag with `: ` is quoted, a portfolio tag reworded (C130)."
  },
